WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.870
- I love a good collaboration y'all

00:00:01.870 --> 00:00:04.920
and my next guests are
Grammy winning country stars

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:07.690
who are set to release an
album of great collaborations

00:00:07.690 --> 00:00:09.400
on November 13th, which is a great day

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:10.870
'cause it's my sister's birthday.

00:00:10.870 --> 00:00:14.130
It's called "Every Road" here we go.

00:00:14.130 --> 00:00:15.720
I grew up on these guys.

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:16.970
What!

00:00:16.970 --> 00:00:19.580
Please, welcome Marty
Raybon, and Mike McGuire

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:21.290
from Shenandoah.
(audience cheering)

00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:23.280
Also welcome the awesome band

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:25.600
who joined them for one of
the tracks on their album,

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:28.050
Hillary Scott, Dave
Haywood, and Charles Kelley

00:00:28.050 --> 00:00:30.198
from Lady A, give it up!

00:00:30.198 --> 00:00:33.198
(audience cheering)

00:00:34.850 --> 00:00:35.863
What's up y'all!

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:38.220
- Hi.

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:39.273
- I miss Nashville.

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:41.240
It is so great to see you.

00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:43.370
It's been a long, long time actually,

00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:45.100
since I've seen y'all, I feel like.

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:46.070
- Yes, it has.

00:00:46.070 --> 00:00:49.413
I feel like a couple of years.

00:00:49.413 --> 00:00:52.230
I think probably it's been
too long. We missed ya.

00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:53.240
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:53.240 --> 00:00:54.630
I feel like-
- Probably, when we made that

00:00:54.630 --> 00:00:57.150
tribute to Reba McEntire, right?

00:00:57.150 --> 00:00:58.780
- Maybe, yeah, that's what I was thinking.

00:00:58.780 --> 00:01:00.410
Maybe it is that, Yeah.

00:01:00.410 --> 00:01:02.590
And I guess we always run
into each other's shows.

00:01:02.590 --> 00:01:03.683
Yeah, yeah.

00:01:04.580 --> 00:01:06.300
How's Kelly doing Dave?

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:08.180
- Ah, she's good. She says hello.

00:01:08.180 --> 00:01:09.880
I know last time we were hanging out,

00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:13.040
we were playing pool against
you at a dinner party.

00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:14.600
But we're doing good, hanging in there.

00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:15.433
- I know.

00:01:15.433 --> 00:01:18.020
And I actually saw y'all video.

00:01:18.020 --> 00:01:19.390
Y'all are doing videos together

00:01:19.390 --> 00:01:20.640
and you're so hysterical.

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:21.840
- [Dave] That's my wife and I.

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:23.378
- You in for funniest couple.

00:01:23.378 --> 00:01:24.486
(laughs)

00:01:24.486 --> 00:01:25.920
- [Dave] Ah, thank you.

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:26.880
We've gotten very bored.

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:28.480
We've gotten very bored.

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:31.583
- It entertained me for
a long time, my friend.

00:01:32.530 --> 00:01:34.870
Well, Jamie and Kristen are
y'all country music fans?

00:01:34.870 --> 00:01:36.280
Jamie, I'll start with you.

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:38.850
- Oh, yes. Are you kidding?

00:01:38.850 --> 00:01:40.273
I married a musician?

00:01:40.273 --> 00:01:41.999
You'd know.
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:41.999 --> 00:01:43.310
Well, no, but I mean, no, no.

00:01:43.310 --> 00:01:45.580
I'm saying he did a
different kind of music.

00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:47.300
I mean, he was known for spinal tap

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:49.360
and being sort of a fake rock guitars,

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:51.850
but he's a classical musician

00:01:51.850 --> 00:01:54.610
and yes, devoted to music.

00:01:54.610 --> 00:01:57.530
In fact, if you haven't
seen it, everybody,

00:01:57.530 --> 00:02:01.560
the PBS Ken Burns country
music documentary series,

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:04.160
is one of the greatest experiences

00:02:04.160 --> 00:02:06.246
you will ever have in your entire lives.

00:02:06.246 --> 00:02:07.476
- Agreed. Agreed.

00:02:07.476 --> 00:02:08.710
I love that you saw that.
- I agree, I watched that,

00:02:08.710 --> 00:02:10.760
that was spot on.

00:02:10.760 --> 00:02:11.998
- Kristen, do you like
you're in Nashville now.

00:02:11.998 --> 00:02:13.390
- Exactly, I tell what,

00:02:13.390 --> 00:02:15.240
being in Nashville now
for about eight years,

00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:17.610
I've learned to start
loving country music.

00:02:17.610 --> 00:02:18.930
Didn't think I would ever be that girl,

00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:20.390
but I am a big fan now (laughs).

00:02:20.390 --> 00:02:21.563
- Yes. They'll suck you in.

00:02:21.563 --> 00:02:22.890
It's the lifestyle too.

00:02:22.890 --> 00:02:24.720
Everybody it's so nice.

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:27.630
So Jamie, is it true that you
once wrote a country song?

00:02:27.630 --> 00:02:29.333
I heard that you maybe wrote one.

00:02:30.390 --> 00:02:33.420
- I may have written a country music song.

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:36.680
It may be called "Don't
Treat Your Man Too Rough".

00:02:36.680 --> 00:02:37.783
It's sort of a-

00:02:37.783 --> 00:02:41.134
(Kelly laughs)

00:02:41.134 --> 00:02:43.570
It's a little bit about like,

00:02:43.570 --> 00:02:45.650
we need to like give them a bit of a break

00:02:45.650 --> 00:02:48.323
because we re bro beat them a bit.

00:02:49.270 --> 00:02:50.390
You know what Kelly?

00:02:50.390 --> 00:02:51.760
I'm gonna send it to you,

00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:53.680
off air I will send it to you

00:02:53.680 --> 00:02:56.100
and see maybe we can collaborate.

00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:58.100
- Okay. And maybe at the end
they can twist and be like,

00:02:58.100 --> 00:02:59.510
nah, nevermind I was right.

00:02:59.510 --> 00:03:01.677
(laughs)

00:03:03.230 --> 00:03:04.100
So Mike and Marty,

00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:05.890
tell us about the new album "Every Road".

00:03:05.890 --> 00:03:07.490
I think I saw, did Blake Shelton,

00:03:07.490 --> 00:03:09.380
did he tweet about it, he's on it as well?

00:03:09.380 --> 00:03:10.720
- Yeah, Blake Shelton (indistinct).

00:03:10.720 --> 00:03:12.830
- Yeah, that's cool.

00:03:12.830 --> 00:03:13.930
- It literally is a,

00:03:13.930 --> 00:03:15.810
it's a collaboration record where

00:03:16.750 --> 00:03:17.973
Dierks Bentley is on it.

00:03:19.090 --> 00:03:20.940
Cody Johnson from Texas,

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:23.210
a buddy of ours that we met down there,

00:03:23.210 --> 00:03:25.300
Brad Paisley's on it.

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:27.120
We got Ashley McBryde.

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:29.113
She's a part of it, part of the peers.

00:03:30.150 --> 00:03:34.173
You know, it's just a record that really,

00:03:35.150 --> 00:03:37.040
it was something that we wanted to do

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:39.060
as far as trying to do a record

00:03:39.060 --> 00:03:42.030
and to invite people to be a part of it.

00:03:42.030 --> 00:03:43.980
But we didn't wanna do a record

00:03:43.980 --> 00:03:45.690
that was the greatest hits.

00:03:45.690 --> 00:03:46.720
- Yeah.
- Like in other words,

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:48.210
you know, everybody come over

00:03:48.210 --> 00:03:49.670
and do "Two Dozen Roses" with us.

00:03:49.670 --> 00:03:52.710
Everybody come to "Church
on Cumberland Road".

00:03:52.710 --> 00:03:54.450
We wanted to have new material

00:03:54.450 --> 00:03:56.560
because this actually is
the first record we'd done

00:03:56.560 --> 00:03:58.093
in 20 years that we've had,

00:03:58.093 --> 00:04:00.960
the end of the whole album,
it's all new material.

00:04:00.960 --> 00:04:01.793
- Yeah.

00:04:01.793 --> 00:04:04.470
- And the first time I
believe it's ever been done

00:04:04.470 --> 00:04:06.090
with guests artists.

00:04:06.090 --> 00:04:10.343
And the great thing about
what Lady A had sent us,

00:04:11.700 --> 00:04:15.560
they had sent us the tune
that they had written

00:04:15.560 --> 00:04:18.310
and that was a wonderful piece of music.

00:04:18.310 --> 00:04:20.720
And when we cut the tracks
and got the vocals on it,

00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:21.970
and then all of a sudden

00:04:21.970 --> 00:04:25.840
when the Lady A put their
vocals on there as well,

00:04:25.840 --> 00:04:27.040
mainly just listened to it.

00:04:27.040 --> 00:04:29.770
It make you take back
stuff you ain't stole.

00:04:29.770 --> 00:04:32.110
I mean, them cats can forever more sing.

00:04:32.110 --> 00:04:33.490
I mean they just can

00:04:34.360 --> 00:04:36.200
and this whole album literally

00:04:37.430 --> 00:04:40.950
it's literally a gathering
of that type of material.

00:04:40.950 --> 00:04:42.750
- I love, that's my
favorite kind of record.

00:04:42.750 --> 00:04:43.600
That's what I grew up on.

00:04:43.600 --> 00:04:45.260
And so I'm really excited about it.

00:04:45.260 --> 00:04:47.300
Lady, how'd y'all get involved?

00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:50.710
- Yeah, we did that show
and I kinda geeked out

00:04:50.710 --> 00:04:52.110
on these guys, honestly.

00:04:52.110 --> 00:04:54.410
I mean, we grew up on this music

00:04:54.410 --> 00:04:55.410
and I'm not gonna lie,

00:04:55.410 --> 00:04:57.060
I had a little bit of

00:04:58.004 --> 00:05:00.090
a real big fan moment backstage

00:05:01.470 --> 00:05:04.047
and Marty said, "Hey, we're
gonna be working on a record.

00:05:04.047 --> 00:05:06.500
"We should do some, you know,
we should exchange numbers."

00:05:06.500 --> 00:05:08.610
And he never let up. And it was great.

00:05:08.610 --> 00:05:11.123
And then you just started
kinda snowballing,

00:05:13.128 --> 00:05:14.410
'cause that's one of
the things you can have

00:05:14.410 --> 00:05:15.360
these conversations,

00:05:15.360 --> 00:05:18.819
but for it to really come together

00:05:18.819 --> 00:05:19.820
in to fruition

00:05:19.820 --> 00:05:22.920
in the way that they got
all these amazing artists,

00:05:22.920 --> 00:05:25.100
I mean, we really feel
blessed to be a part of it.

00:05:25.100 --> 00:05:28.001
So this is a really cool
project to be a part of.

00:05:28.001 --> 00:05:30.410
I think it could literally,

00:05:30.410 --> 00:05:32.810
just knowing the other
artists that are on it,

00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:34.520
this could be a Grammy winning

00:05:36.130 --> 00:05:37.910
collaboration project

00:05:37.910 --> 00:05:39.680
and I'm just so proud
of being a part of it.

00:05:39.680 --> 00:05:40.513
- Yeah.

00:05:41.410 --> 00:05:45.070
I can only imagine too,
like being such a fan of it.

00:05:45.070 --> 00:05:46.290
I grew up on Shenandoah too.

00:05:46.290 --> 00:05:49.330
So, I can't imagine being
such a fan of someone

00:05:49.330 --> 00:05:50.350
and then getting to do that.

00:05:50.350 --> 00:05:52.760
I mean I can, I got to do
that actually with Reba

00:05:52.760 --> 00:05:53.670
who's one of my favorite people.

00:05:53.670 --> 00:05:56.590
But it's such a different feeling,

00:05:56.590 --> 00:05:58.460
especially you wrote the
song that they're singing,

00:05:58.460 --> 00:05:59.890
which is what y'all did as well.

00:05:59.890 --> 00:06:02.520
It's such a different feeling
of like, "Oh my gosh."

00:06:02.520 --> 00:06:04.220
It's like it doesn't matter
everything that's happened.

00:06:04.220 --> 00:06:07.263
This is like such a cool
moment for 10 year old me.

00:06:08.611 --> 00:06:10.460
And it's just a really
cool thing to be on such

00:06:10.460 --> 00:06:13.010
a cool collaborative project
that you'll put together.

00:06:13.010 --> 00:06:15.450
So Lady A and Shenandoah
are gonna perform later

00:06:15.450 --> 00:06:16.550
in the show.
(audience cheering)

00:06:16.550 --> 00:06:17.597
Shenandoah's new album

00:06:17.597 --> 00:06:20.760
"Every Road" is out November
13th, my sister's birthday.

00:06:20.760 --> 00:06:21.717
It's a great day.

